Hi there,

I am very sorry to say, that this bug report isn't based on the last three
patches on nethack, but I had such a great and long game, that I didn't want
to risc loosing it. I've got nethack 3.1.1 on Interactive Unix 3.2.2

If some bugs are gone, don't bother.

- Kicking objects in walls let the dungeon collapse

- The dungeon also collapsed, when I dropped my Mjollnir on a vault's wall;
  the Guard came and restored the wall. It may also be the the fact, that
  the guard crossed my digged path.

- A friend of mine lost his wand of wishing by a dungeon collapse in the
  castle. He didn't pick it up but collected the other items first.
  Elbereth was still scribbled at the place the wand has been.

- I had a similar problem. My dungeon didn't collapse, but I got a
  memory fault the moment I went up the stairs, the wand of wishing in my
  bag of holding. Restoring the .e.z File gave me back the dungeon, but the
  castle level was explored and all the collected items I found there were
  gone out of my pack. My armor and weapons, which went a little rusty
  while fighting in the castle were restored to the point when I first
  entered the castle.

- Here is one: If you buy yourself AC, the AC goes away, if you pray and your
  god gives you the gift of protection. The gift of my god made my AC go
  from -44 to -30. The protection should have been added to the protection
  I bought and not replaced.

- My friend choked on a fruit potion, when he was not satiated. This only
  happened once.

- Cursed bags of holding may contain memory errors. As soon as you step on
  them (not blind, not floating), you see objects vanish. Looting them
  reveals the error.

- A Memory error duplicated his bag of holding while it was in a box and
  he had some named weapons twice.

- A pointer problem let me kill the Master Thief twice. Also the gnomish
  mines after a certain time were unexplored from the point the shops start.
  Before that, I really made a great mess inside with keystone kops etc.
  Maybe it has something to do with lots of information in a level.

- Whenever I am in a rogue level, I have to switch to !ibm graphics.
  First the graphic is scrambled
  (room walls sometimes step 1 to the right) and then it happened, that the
  game scrambled its item colors, even after saving and reloading. It had
  the effect, that some items looked like ghosts and turned to their normal
  shape, when ibm was turned off, for example armor was invisible.

- When I died in the endgame (thank you for this great challenge; I thought
  I couldn't die any more), the message presenting my Max Level was
  wrong. It said max level 30 but my max level was 56. However in the
  score list the correct max level is shown.

Apart from that, nethack looks as beautiful as ever :-)

Here I got some hints, which would be helpful with bag of holdings and piles
in general.

How about :?
if you are standing on a pile and only want to see the scrolls?

It would be great if the objects could be presented in a way like the
newsreader nn presents its messages and that you can choose directly, what
item you want to pick up. It is a little annoying if you have a 10 page
armor pile laying at your feet and your shield of reflection is on the
last page.

I would also like a classification of armor. [s for shoes, [h for helmets,
[g for gloves etc.  :[g  would only look at gloves. Also a sort pile option
could help.

Since using the bag of holding takes only one turn, I would like a feature,
that after putting something in, I want to take something out again. During
fights I sometimes miss the item I want and loose a turn.

I also want to check my inventory while working with the bag or chest.

One small thing. When starting a game in explorer mode, nethack asks me, if
I want my savefile preserved. When I answer y, nethack writes it out again.
With big savefiles this takes a long time. Meanwhile the message is still
displayed and nothing happens. Maybe a "Please wait..." would help, or
better yet, don't erase the savefile in the first place if in Explorer Mode.

Ok, so much for that. I hope this helps.

